* kindling proof model
*
* 2 variables, 2 constraints
*
* --- x1 in [0, 1], the model's a ---
* x1 = 1*x1b0
*
* x1ge{v} means x1 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x1ge{v} ==> 1*x1b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x1ge{v} <== 1*x1b0 >= v.
@x1ge1_up @x1ge1_dn x1ge1 <==> 1 x1b0 >= 1 ;
* x1eq{v} means x1 = v, which is x1ge{v} and not x1ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x1eq0_up @x1eq0_dn x1eq0 <==> 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1eq1_up @x1eq1_dn x1eq1 <==> 1 x1ge1 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x2 in [0, 1], the model's b ---
* x2 = 1*x2b0
*
* x2ge{v} means x2 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x2ge{v} ==> 1*x2b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x2ge{v} <== 1*x2b0 >= v.
@x2ge1_up @x2ge1_dn x2ge1 <==> 1 x2b0 >= 1 ;
* x2eq{v} means x2 = v, which is x2ge{v} and not x2ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x2eq0_up @x2eq0_dn x2eq0 <==> 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2eq1_up @x2eq1_dn x2eq1 <==> 1 x2ge1 >= 1 ;
*
* table(x1, x2) with 2 tuples
@tbl1_sel 1 c1t0 1 c1t1 >= 1 ;
@tbl1t0 c1t0 ==> 1 x1eq0 1 x2eq0 >= 2 ;
@tbl1t1 c1t1 ==> 1 x1eq1 1 x2eq1 >= 2 ;
*
* table(x1, x2) with 2 tuples
@tbl2_sel 1 c2t0 1 c2t1 >= 1 ;
@tbl2t0 c2t0 ==> 1 x1eq0 1 x2eq1 >= 2 ;
@tbl2t1 c2t1 ==> 1 x1eq1 1 x2eq0 >= 2 ;
